   is another dequeue, often another session, sometimes another process and
   another backend — so the wire cannot be the sending engine's own source
   language. It was: this line built `_scxml_params({...})`, Lua source, and
   the receiving `set_current_event` ran it to get the value back. That made
   the payload EXECUTABLE at the receiving end (measured 2026-08-17: a host
   payload `(function() ... end)()` ran in the session's globals) and made
   `_event.data` type-dependent on which backend sent it (`2 + 3` arrived as
   5 here and as the string "2 + 3" on cpp, which already shipped JSON).

